Install and update (macOS)
--------------------------
Open the .dmg and drag Ssx3.app to Applications, replacing the old one for
an update. The game files are inside the app. To uninstall, drag the app to
the Trash; your saves stay in Application Support.

The app is signed ad hoc on the Mac that built it, not notarized. On
another Mac, Gatekeeper may refuse it: right-click > Open once, or run
  xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/Ssx3.app

To keep saves and settings somewhere else, set SSX3_DATA_DIR to that folder
before starting the game.

Settings
--------
This build has no options file. Launcher settings are KEY=value lines in
config/launch.env in ~/Library/Application Support/Ssx3; the app's
Contents/Resources/launch.env.default lists the defaults.

Controls
--------
Use a controller (Xbox, PlayStation or another SDL-supported pad); it is
player 1. The game reads only the pad.

Speed
-----
The game steps a fixed amount per frame. On a machine that cannot keep up,
races play in slow motion but correctly.

Known gaps on the Mac
---------------------
This is an early port. It has been tested with a scripted controller from
the title screen into a race on Metal; a full play-through has not been
tried.
